  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "Backwards reception and shot",
  "description": "Split the players into two queues, A and B, by the boards just below the centre line. Two passers, C and D, stand in the middle with balls. A cone stands on each side a way up towards the goal. Goalkeeper in goal.\n\nA skates forwards at high speed towards the cone, turns at the cone and carries on backwards. C passes and A receives the ball while skating backwards, turns forwards with the ball and shoots at goal. B starts when A has received and gets their pass from D. Join the back of the same queue afterwards.\n\nChange direction after a while so the turns are made both ways, and swap passers. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "High tempo into the cone – the turn is made at speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Stick on the ice and eyes on the passer while skating backwards."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Receive the ball in front of your body so you can turn at once."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Turn forwards with the first stride and shoot before the goalkeeper is set."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
